3-     3	
4-     4	Validates a Pair-Rail verdict artifact (`.claude/governance/
5-     5	pair-rail-verdict-<release-tag>.md`) per R1 S-Sec-3 replay defense +
6:     6	R1 S-Sec-4 inputs_hash determinism + R1 C5 Codex CLI pin enforcement
7-     7	+ R1 S-QA-Unseen-2 distinct VERDICT_EXPIRED exit code.
8-     8	
9-     9	## Usage
10-    10	
--
14-    14	      --release-tag ${GITHUB_REF_NAME} \\
15-    15	      --max-age-hours 24 \\
16-    16	      --recompute-inputs-hash \\
17-    17	      --codex-cli-pin-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \\
18:    18	      --codex-pin-manifest-file .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json \\
19:    19	      --inputs-hash-paths-file .claude/governance/pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt
20-    20	
21-    21	## ADR-182 payload pin (PLAN-163 T5.2)
22-    22	
23:    23	`--codex-pin-manifest-file` enforces the payload pin: the verdict
24-    24	envelope MUST declare `tool_versions.codex_target_triple` (the platform
25-    25	triple of the run that generated the verdict) and
26-    26	`tool_versions.codex_payload_sha256` (sha256 of the NATIVE codex
27-    27	payload for that triple — NOT the npm JS launcher). The validator
28-    28	compares the declared sha against
29:    29	`manifest.payloads[<triple>].sha256`. Fail-CLOSED: missing fields,
30:    30	triple absent from the manifest, malformed entry, or sha mismatch →
31-    31	VERDICT_INVALID (3). Manifest file unreadable → infra (1). The legacy
32-    32	`--codex-cli-binary-sha256-file` launcher-hash pin is retained only for
33-    33	pre-ADR-182 tags; the live pin file is a comment-only tombstone, which
34-    34	that legacy path treats as "no pin" (skip).
35-    35	
36:    36	## parent_sha vs commit_sha (S104 redesign)
37-    37	
38-    38	The legacy `--commit-sha` arg + verdict `commit_sha:` field bound the
39-    39	verdict to a SHA the verdict commit itself produced — an unsolvable
40-    40	self-reference (`pair-rail-verdict-vX.md` cannot declare its own commit
41-    41	SHA because that SHA is only known AFTER the verdict file is committed).
42-    42	The v1.16.0 GA ceremony bridged this via `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1`
43-    43	transition mode, which silently disabled the bind.
44-    44	
45:    45	`parent_sha:` solves it cleanly. The verdict declares the commit it was
46-    46	generated AGAINST (the parent of the verdict-file commit). That value is
47-    47	known when the verdict is authored (it's `git rev-parse HEAD` before the
48-    48	verdict commit). Step 15 validates against `git log -n1 --format=%H --
49-    49	<verdict-file>` parent, which is observable + immutable.
--
51-    51	Backward-compat: when only `commit_sha:` (legacy) is present and
52-    52	`--parent-sha` is empty, the bind is skipped with an ADVISORY (matches
53-    53	prior CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 behavior). Legacy verdicts for
54-    54	already-shipped tags (v1.16.0 etc.) keep their existing semantics; new
55:    55	verdicts use `parent_sha:`.
56-    56	
57-    57	## Exit codes
58-    58	
59-    59	- 0: verdict valid; release proceeds.
60-    60	- 1: infra error (file missing / unparseable / etc.); release.yml
61-    61	     decides based on CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL.
62-    62	- 2: VERDICT_EXPIRED — distinct from infra-error per R1 S-QA-Unseen-2.
63-    63	     Release.yml can route this to a "verdict regen" branch.
64:    64	- 3: VERDICT_INVALID — release_tag mismatch / parent_sha mismatch /
65:    65	     inputs_hash mismatch / pin mismatch / signature missing. Release
66-    66	     MUST stop here.
67-    67	
68-    68	stdlib only. Python ≥3.9.
