- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:143` — Commit 1 is not actually closed: directory entries match arbitrary descendants, and line 198 recursively stages them. A nested look-alike under `repass-rc3-cures/`, `repass-ga-rc2-NOGO/`, or `staged-w3/` rides commit 1; because `parent_sha` is that commit, the delta guard never sees it. Minimal fix: establish file-level set equality for every directory against reviewed manifests and stage only literal files.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:78`, `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:147` — Authorization decisions depend on mutable control files outside the signed manifest sets. RC3 selects the authoritative round from `RAIL-STATUS.txt`; GA reuses evidence based on `PROVENANCE-ga.md`, while `run-ga-repass.sh:185` excludes provenance from `MANIFEST-ga.sha256`. An edited status can select an earlier GO, or stale internally consistent evidence can be paired with rewritten provenance and reused. If these files are already in the manifests, the templates instead fail guard set equality because they omit them. Minimal fix: manifest a machine-readable final-status/anchor record and verify manifest content and exact set before either GO selection or reuse.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:100` — The advertised pre-commit-1 rerun is broken. After line 174 copies any cure—or after all copies succeed and a local gate fails—the next invocation requires every live file to match the pre-cure `BASELINE.sha256` and aborts. Minimal fix: install an exit restoration trap from `EXPECTED_HEAD`, or accept only per-file baseline/pack hashes and idempotently reapply the complete pack while rejecting every third state.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:151` — An early redactor/cap/output failure leaves `payload-ga-N.raw.txt` in `repass-ga/`; it is moved only at line 170. The next `OWNER-GA-CUT.sh` invocation rejects that raw file during G0 and cannot resume. Minimal fix: use an EXIT trap that quarantines raw payloads under unique names, then rerun the exact output-set check immediately before commit 1.

- P2 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/pair-rail-verdict-v1.3.0.TEMPLATE.md:66` — The signed GA record still claims main was frozen from the rc.2 cut, although the rc.3 cure commits necessarily changed main. `OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:2` repeats the stale promotion label. Minimal fix: consistently say the GA promotes rc.3 and that the freeze starts at the rc.3 cut.

The input hashes and manifest basenames are coherent, but the P1 closure and resume defects must be corrected before the rc.3 cut.

VERDICT: NO-GOP1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:140,245`  
The reviewed provenance binds only the cure pack’s manifest, baseline, modes, and anchor. Ceremony scripts, templates, sentinel draft, and morning instructions are accepted solely by pathname. After this review, a same-path edit—such as reverting `OWNER-GA-CUT.sh` to rc.2 or altering a verdict template—passes both G0 checks and is committed as reviewed content.  
Minimal fix: add a closed SHA-256 manifest for every reviewed ceremony file, pin that manifest in the manifest-verified provenance, and verify file hashes both at G0 and immediately before staging.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:145`  
Invalid existing GA evidence triggers regeneration, but the runner redirects to fixed output paths before rejecting symlinks or other non-regular entries. An untracked `repass-ga/PROVENANCE-ga.md` symlink to `CHANGELOG.md`, for example, is pathname-allowlisted by GA G0; validation returns false, then this redirection truncates `CHANGELOG.md`. The run eventually stops, but the supposedly resumable pre-commit state is already corrupted.  
Minimal fix: before any evidence write, enumerate every fixed GA output and abort on symlinks or non-regular existing entries; only regular expected outputs may be removed and regenerated.

Both findings must be cured and re-reviewed before the rc.3 ceremony freezes these scripts onto main.

